course: dictionary
lesson: 5562
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Lent is one of them. The context, meaning the words around it, tells you which meaning the writer means. «I lent him my pen» is about borrowing and lending, so lent is the past of lend: you gave something to someone for a short time, expecting to get it back.
explain: Lent with a capital L is a time in the Christian year, the forty days before Easter. The clues are the capital letter and words like churches, Christians and Easter. «Many churches change the colours of their cloths with the seasons, for example purple for Advent and Lent» is about church seasons, not borrowing.
explain: Look for clues near the word. If the sentence is about a pen, a book or money being borrowed, think lend. If it is about Easter, churches or giving up sweets, think Lent. Then try your meaning in the sentence to check that it makes sense.
fact: Lent is the past of lend, so it is used for things already lent for a short time: I lent my bike to Sam yesterday.
fact: Lent (capital L) is the forty days before Easter, when many Christians pray and give something up, like sweets.
fact: Lent starts on Ash Wednesday, and Pancake Day (Shrove Tuesday) is the day before.
fact: «In Lent many Christians give something up or take something good on.»
fact: «Lent is forty days not counting Sundays, so from Ash Wednesday to Easter Day is longer than forty days on the calendar.»
exercise: «I lent him my pen.» What does lent mean here? | Gave away for ever | *Gave for a short time, expecting it back | Forty days before Easter | Took something without asking
exercise: «Lent is forty days before Easter.» Which word is the clue that Lent means the church season? | Borrow | Pen | Bike | *Easter
exercise: «She lent a hand with the dishes.» What does lent a hand mean? | *Helped | Gave a hand-shaped sweet | Hurt her hand | Let someone borrow a hand
test: What is the day before Ash Wednesday? | *Pancake Day | Easter Day | Christmas Day | Boxing Day
test: «I lent it to Ava yesterday.» What does lent mean in this sentence? | Prayed for forty days | Forty days before Easter | Given back at once | *Past of lend: gave for a short time
exam: Which sentence uses Lent with a capital L for the church season? | He lent the book to his cousin. | She lent a hand. | *In Lent many Christians give something up. | I lent my ruler to Sam.
